    "summary": "Cloth; composed of nine narrow strips each about 5 1/2 inches wide, of hand-spun cotton, either white or dyed indigo; hand-woven and hand-sewn along the selvedges. Each strip has the same structure which forms a pattern that runs across the cloth. The warp is indigo, the weft is of indigo or white cotton, with supplementary indigo weft threads that forms nine bands of pattern. The warp ends have been left to form a fringe.",
